---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Data Deletion Instructions" description="How to request deletion of your data from Yield Force: for customers who messaged a business that uses Yield Force, for businesses using Yield Force, and for connected Google Ads and Meta accounts.">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-16">
    <div class="mb-12 border-b border-slate-800 pb-8">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full border border-blue-500/30 bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-400 text-xs font-medium mb-4">
        Your data, your choice
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight mb-3">Data Deletion Instructions</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-slate-400 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        This page explains how to have your data deleted from Yield Force, and how to remove Yield Force's access to your accounts. Yield Force is operated by Gaia Holdings Limited, registered in Uganda.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-300">

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">1. You messaged a business that uses Yield Force</h2>
        <p>If you chatted with an online store or business on WhatsApp, Instagram or Facebook Messenger, that business decides how your messages are used and is responsible for your data. Yield Force processes the conversation on the business's behalf.</p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li><strong class="text-white">Option A:</strong> contact the business directly and ask it to delete your data. It can action the request through Yield Force.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Option B:</strong> email us at <a href="mailto:dev@yieldforce.dev?subject=Data%20deletion%20request" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">dev@yieldforce.dev</a> with the subject <em>Data deletion request</em>. Tell us the name of the business, the channel you used (WhatsApp, Instagram or Facebook), and the phone number or account name you messaged from, so we can find your conversation. We will assist the business in fulfilling your request.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We respond within <strong class="text-white">one calendar month</strong>, free of charge, subject to verifying that the request comes from you.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">2. You are a business using Yield Force</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li><strong class="text-white">Shopify merchants:</strong> uninstalling the Yield Force app from your Shopify Admin triggers Shopify's data erasure notifications. Customer and shop data is purged within <strong class="text-white">30 days</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Direct clients:</strong> email <a href="mailto:dev@yieldforce.dev?subject=Data%20deletion%20request" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">dev@yieldforce.dev</a> with the subject <em>Data deletion request</em> from the address registered on your account.</li>
          <li><strong class="text-white">Conversation retention:</strong> conversations are permanently purged after 90 days by default, or sooner if you configure it.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">3. Disconnect Google Ads</h2>
        <p>You can disconnect Google Ads at any time under Configuration, Channels in Yield Force, which removes the stored connection and token. You can also revoke access directly at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>. See <a href="/privacy#google-user-data" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">Google User Data</a> in our Privacy Policy.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">4. Remove Yield Force from your Facebook or Instagram account</h2>
        <p>If you are a business that connected a Facebook Page, Instagram account or WhatsApp Business Account, you can remove Yield Force's access at any time in your Meta <a href="https://www.facebook.com/settings?tab=business_tools" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">Business Integrations settings</a>. To also have your data deleted, follow section 2 above.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="space-y-3 border-t border-slate-800 pt-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">Questions</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:dev@yieldforce.dev" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">dev@yieldforce.dev</a>. More detail on what we store and for how long is in our <a href="/privacy" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/data" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline">Data Handling Disclosure</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
